# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# The utility is optional (UP). The test runs it with an input that is not a
# terminal, which the page says must fail; the session itself needs two
# terminals and cannot be scripted.

assertion  XCU.talk.001
anchor     utilities/talk.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/talk.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       UP
says       When standard input is not a terminal, talk writes a diagnostic
           message and exits with a status above zero.
test       t/001-stdin-not-terminal.sh

assertion  XCU.talk.002
anchor     utilities/talk.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/talk.html#OPERANDS
class      untestable
says       talk sends its connection request to the address and, once the other
           side answers, shows the two parties' typing in separate regions.
reason     It is a screen program that needs a terminal on each side and a
           second login to answer, which a script run by the driver lacks.
